# the master knobs: the starting assignments, the knob rows in GLO, the MASTER pot as an effect, masks and macros (SEL opens a row's details)
expectknob 0 1
expectknob 1 4
expectknob 2 2
expectknob 3 2
expectfx 1 0 64
# SELECT runs the master FX (drive until GLO says otherwise), PRESETS is the DJ filter (the middle is off), ALGORITHM its resonance
turn SELECT 5
expectfx 2 0 10
turn PRESET -5
expectfx 1 0 54
turn ALGO 4
expectfx 1 1 48
# GLO: the MASTER KNOB row is the third (TEMPO, MASTER FX, MASTER KNOB ...); K2 changes what it does: VOLUME -> FILTER DJ
tap GLO
expect view 3
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectknob 0 2
shot knobs_glo.png
# the pot is the filter only once it has been moved
master 2048
wait 100
expectfx 1 0 54
master 3000
wait 100
expectfx 1 0 109
# SEL on the row: the tracks the filter acts on (black keys; the MUTE key = all)
tap SEL
expect view 6
shot knobs_fx.png
tapkey b2
expectmask 1 4
tapkey b4
expectmask 1 20
tapkey b2
expectmask 1 16
tapkey b10
expectmask 1 0
expect trk 0
# SELECT KNOB row: K2 one step back from the master FX is a macro; SEL opens its targets: track 6 (the 303), its first pot
tap GLO
turn K1 1
turn K2 -1
expectknob 1 3
tap SEL
expect view 6
tapkey b5
expect trk 0
shot knobs_macro.png
turn SELECT 10
expectpar 5 0 20
# the same macro aimed at the track's LEVEL (K4 to the left end), and inverted with SEL
turn K3 1
turn K3 -1
turn K4 -30
turn SELECT 15
expectlevel 5 50
tap SEL
turn SELECT 5
expectlevel 5 67
# a row with nothing to set says so (PRESETS KNOB is the DJ filter: it has tracks; ALGO KNOB too; a VOLUME knob has none)
tap GLO
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
expectknob 0 2
